<figure class="execution-example" aria-label="Illustrative buy order: the unweighted mean of fill prices is 101 dollars, while the quantity-weighted execution price is 101 dollars and 80 cents">
  <div class="example-head">
    <span class="example-label">Illustrative buy order · USD</span>
    <strong class="example-title">More shares give a fill more weight.</strong>
    <p>Two fills for our own buy order, in the same security and currency.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="fill-ledger" role="group" aria-label="Our two executions">
    <div class="fill-row">
      <span class="fill-name"><span class="fill-mark first" aria-hidden="true"></span><strong>Fill A</strong></span>
      <span class="fill-detail"><span class="qf-figure">100</span> shares at <span class="qf-figure">$100</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="fill-row">
      <span class="fill-name"><span class="fill-mark second" aria-hidden="true"></span><strong>Fill B</strong></span>
      <span class="fill-detail"><span class="qf-figure">900</span> shares at <span class="qf-figure">$102</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="order-totals">
      <div><span>Total shares</span><strong class="qf-figure">1,000</strong></div>
      <div><span>Total cost</span><strong class="qf-figure">$101,800</strong></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="price-comparison">
    <div class="price-method unweighted">
      <span class="method-label">Ignores the share quantities</span>
      <strong class="method-name">Unweighted fill-price mean</strong>
      <span class="price-value qf-figure">$101.00</span>
      <div class="weight-bar equal" aria-hidden="true"><span class="first"></span><span class="second"></span></div>
      <span class="weight-label">Each fill gets half the weight.</span>
      <span class="price-formula qf-figure">($100 + $102) ÷ 2</span>
    </div>
    <div class="price-method weighted">
      <span class="method-label">Weights each fill by its shares</span>
      <strong class="method-name">Quantity-weighted execution price</strong>
      <span class="price-value qf-figure">$101.80</span>
      <div class="weight-bar by-quantity" aria-hidden="true"><span class="first"></span><span class="second"></span></div>
      <span class="weight-label">Fill B gets nine times the weight.</span>
      <span class="price-formula"><span class="qf-figure">$101,800</span> ÷ <span class="qf-figure">1,000</span> shares</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cost-calculation">
    <span>Total cost comes from both fills</span>
    <span class="cost-formula"><span class="qf-figure">(100 × $100)</span><span class="qf-figure"> + (900 × $102)</span><span class="qf-figure"> = $101,800</span></span>
  </div>
  <figcaption>For our executions, average price is total cost divided by total shares. This measures our own fills, not market VWAP.</figcaption>
</figure>

